{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (confirmed at runtime): the close landed-work precheck's commit scan (_referencing_commit_exists, src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:149-175) calls the shared resolver resolve_ticket_id (src/rebar/_ids.py:191) for EVERY candidate ref extracted from EVERY reachable commit message. resolve_ticket_id prints ambiguity diagnostics directly to stderr (src/rebar/_ids.py:229-233 for 8-hex, :249-254 for alias, :270-274 'Ambiguous prefix ... matches multiple tickets'). Reproduced: a tracker with two tickets sharing a 4-hex prefix + a historical commit whose subject leads with that prefix -> scanning prints 'Error: Ambiguous prefix 2f3c matches multiple tickets: ...' while the scan still returns True for a full-ID trailer elsewhere in history. The return value is unaffected (ambiguous resolves return None either way), so this is pure diagnostic noise -- gate semantics are unchanged by the fix. Fix plan: add a keyword-only quiet=False parameter to resolve_ticket_id gating the three stderr prints; pass quiet=True ONLY from _referencing_commit_exists's scan loop. Explicit user-supplied ambiguous target ids (resolved elsewhere without quiet) keep full diagnostics."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858304294549001,"uuid":"2a87f0cf-b33a-4332-83dd-e140fa4a837d"}